  <h1>OPD Has Foresight: Why Distillation Beats RL and How to Exploit It 3×</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    On-policy distillation (OPD) isn't just "denser supervision" — at the parameter level it locks onto the correct update direction within the first 10% of training, far earlier than RL ever does. This foresight manifests as two measurable properties: <em>functional redundancy avoidance</em> (OPD ignores low-utility layers early) and <em>early low-rank lock-in</em> (its dominant subspaces stabilize fast). EffOPD exploits both to achieve a 3× training speedup with no extra modules.
  </p>
  <div class="post-hero-meta">
